                            "singular",
                            "feminine",
                            "short-form"
                        ],
                        "form": "бестеле́сна"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e4dfb222-eb30-4d30-b137-1052e63889f3",
                        "entry_id": "bc152e89-f202-3d21-b46a-5fdd3396ab2a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "short-form"
                        ],
                        "form": "бестеле́сны"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba78d090-b43d-326f-b860-c43198fa8a10",
                        "entry_id": "bc152e89-f202-3d21-b46a-5fdd3396ab2a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. не имеющий тела, нематериальный, бесплотный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb2407d0-6b40-46c0-b99a-34b7fdf43575",
                                "sense_id": "ba78d090-b43d-326f-b860-c43198fa8a10",
                                "text": "— За всё, что сделал Керн со мной, с вашим отцом, с вами, с теми несчастными головами, которые он воскресил для ада бестелесного существования, он должен понести наказание."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "08f56bbd-4c1c-41f2-8900-9e44b58ffc41",
                                "sense_id": "ba78d090-b43d-326f-b860-c43198fa8a10",
                                "text": "Но, может быть, вы оцените мое напряжённое, всё отмечающее смятение, если я сообщу, что, задев случайно рукой о стул, я не почувствовал прикосновения — так, как если бы был бестелесен."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "46146b91-0e02-4874-9ae6-0497d69f822e",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc152e89-f202-3d21-b46a-5fdd3396ab2a",
                        "source_sense_id": "ba78d090-b43d-326f-b860-c43198fa8a10",
                        "target_lang_word": "bodiless",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bodiless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ce733f6-4caf-3c1c-9bb6-9a3e4443d5f3",
                                        "entry_id": "6371e886-fad8-3653-80f4-bd5875b83e27",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lacking a body; incorporeal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10133b4f-155e-4af2-872d-40e144cc0e7a",
                                                "sense_id": "9ce733f6-4caf-3c1c-9bb6-9a3e4443d5f3",
                                                "text": "Ever and anon the cheek wore a deeper crimson, and the dark eyes filled with sudden fire, as he felt the idea clothe itself in words tangible to the many, as its bodiless presence had previously been to himself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b8c4cfb-81d6-4a45-a71f-eb4a2eadcc08",
                                                "sense_id": "9ce733f6-4caf-3c1c-9bb6-9a3e4443d5f3",
                                                "text": "Be satisfied that I will not have done with thee until I have taken away thy life, and sent thy soul squealing bodiless into the unknown."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e77c0ad1-ff65-4f46-8670-56466c2a57b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc152e89-f202-3d21-b46a-5fdd3396ab2a",
                        "source_sense_id": "ba78d090-b43d-326f-b860-c43198fa8a10",
                        "target_lang_word": "immaterial",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "immaterial",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e143134-7fab-33a0-89c0-71057b9443ed",
                                        "entry_id": "128adf04-3eb2-315a-9632-bb59da4733e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having no matter or substance; incorporeal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a227e55a-8779-4e5a-b26e-17f7d9731cb6",
                                                "sense_id": "9e143134-7fab-33a0-89c0-71057b9443ed",
                                                "text": "Some believe that because ghosts are immaterial, they can pass through walls."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d74a10b-e069-4a58-b6f2-4a6d9acd1278",
                                                "sense_id": "9e143134-7fab-33a0-89c0-71057b9443ed",
                                                "text": "You feel like a disembodied spirit, immaterial; and you seem to be able to touch beauty as though it were a palpable thing; and you feel an intimate communion with the breeze, and with the trees breaking into leaf, and with the iridescence of the river. You feel like God. Can you explain that to me?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57deba1d-968a-3204-8afc-25ac2e1d2778",
                                        "entry_id": "128adf04-3eb2-315a-9632-bb59da4733e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the nature of the soul or spirit; spiritual."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b4e467a-42c9-4814-8132-fae95aabc0a9",
                                                "sense_id": "57deba1d-968a-3204-8afc-25ac2e1d2778",
                                                "text": "[T]here are ſome beings in the vvorld vvhich cannot depend upon matter or motion, i.e. that there are ſome ſpiritual and immaterial ſubstances or Beings […] If there be then ſuch things in the vvorld vvhich matter and motion cannot be the cauſes of, then there are certainly spiritual and immaterial Beings, and that I ſhall make appear both as to the minds of men, and to ſome extraordinary effects vvhich are produced in the vvorld."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a111e26c-7948-32da-a40c-75d75c6b48b4",
                                        "entry_id": "128adf04-3eb2-315a-9632-bb59da4733e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of no importance; inconsequential, insignificant, unimportant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17d7f46b-78f3-4896-b508-a9843debe489",
                                                "sense_id": "a111e26c-7948-32da-a40c-75d75c6b48b4",
                                                "text": "He has also been good enough to recommend to me many tradesmen who are ready to supply these articles in any quantities; each of whom has been here already a dozen times, cap in hand, and vowing that it is quite immaterial when I pay—which is very kind of them; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "911fa998-3706-3931-84a6-4e8fa8b91bd4",
                                        "entry_id": "128adf04-3eb2-315a-9632-bb59da4733e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having or seeming to have very little substance; insubstantial, slight."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd8285c4-9745-4a0f-b9ed-5cb00df35c02",
                                                "sense_id": "911fa998-3706-3931-84a6-4e8fa8b91bd4",
                                                "text": "No, vvhy art thou then exaſperate, thou idle, / immaterial ſkeine of ſleiue ſilke; thou greene ſacenet flap for a ſore eye, thou toſſell of a prodigalls purſe— […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71723bfe-3074-4b78-baf0-60dd389d6f43",
                                                "sense_id": "911fa998-3706-3931-84a6-4e8fa8b91bd4",
                                                "text": "Mr. Woodhouse considered eight persons at dinner together as the utmost that his nerves could bear—and here was a ninth— […] She [Emma] comforted her father better than she could comfort herself, by representing that though he certainly would make them nine, yet he always said so little, that the increase of noise would be very immaterial."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52017334-8893-367e-9691-cc6284459104",
                                        "entry_id": "128adf04-3eb2-315a-9632-bb59da4733e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Especially of evidence; chiefly followed by to: not associated in any way that is important or useful to the context being discussed; irrelevant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d0421fc-013f-48c7-9f49-cfff979c939c",
                                                "sense_id": "52017334-8893-367e-9691-cc6284459104",
                                                "text": "Objection, your Honour! The defendant’s criminal record is immaterial to this case."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30f0db7f-a1a5-4920-b489-157852be9f50",
                                                "sense_id": "52017334-8893-367e-9691-cc6284459104",
                                                "text": "He was perpetually at her side, trying, apparently, to preserve the thread of a disconnected talk, the fate of which was, to judge by her face, profoundly immaterial to the young lady."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "immaterial",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7fdd294d-d9ed-318f-9dd7-a9b848f6392d",
                                        "entry_id": "f5fd35b0-721f-3f92-8de7-ee7faa4e239f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A being or entity having no matter or substance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e691e96-8dfa-3d56-947f-fd791ffe7880",
                                        "entry_id": "f5fd35b0-721f-3f92-8de7-ee7faa4e239f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A thing which is abstract or intangible; (uncountable) chiefly preceded by the: things which are abstract or intangible considered collectively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21f564a7-0af3-4f47-a3c7-35cbbb15d2e8",
                                                "sense_id": "0e691e96-8dfa-3d56-947f-fd791ffe7880",
                                                "text": "Lodge immaterials in thy Head: aſcend unto inviſibles: fill thy Spirit vvith Spirituals, vvith the myſteries of Faith, the magnalities of Religion, and thy Life vvith the Honour of God; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a24c3071-3e2e-4e3a-b668-ca13bc14d91b",
                                                "sense_id": "0e691e96-8dfa-3d56-947f-fd791ffe7880",
                                                "text": "And we do absolutely know that these men's inborn temperaments have remained unchanged through all the vicissitudes of their material affairs. Let us see how it is with their immaterials."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "af3a33fa-1b1c-4dd4-90d6-6d3d5581065e",
                        "source_entry_id": "bc152e89-f202-3d21-b46a-5fdd3396ab2a",
                        "source_sense_id": "ba78d090-b43d-326f-b860-c43198fa8a10",
                        "target_lang_word": "incorporeal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "incorporeal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a251745-1c16-3015-9f03-cf69a5ff664f",
                                        "entry_id": "c6b42b3f-9dcb-3171-81f9-431c3a6d01b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having no material form or physical substance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b1ce51f-ecad-42f7-b806-90194ac2903a",
                                                "sense_id": "6a251745-1c16-3015-9f03-cf69a5ff664f",
                                                "text": "Thus incorporeal spirits to smaller forms / Reduced their shapes immense."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2f76e0c-a850-41c2-80aa-9e276b1156f8",
                                                "sense_id": "6a251745-1c16-3015-9f03-cf69a5ff664f",
                                                "text": "Sense and perception must necessarily proceed from some incorporeal substance within us."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7ddaeef-9351-3bec-980d-2c84827d4082",
                                        "entry_id": "c6b42b3f-9dcb-3171-81f9-431c3a6d01b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to an asset that does not have a material form; such as a patent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "incorporeal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "057fc5d1-b731-319a-9e0b-e38ad2bc3a13",
                                        "entry_id": "619c260b-1dbb-3211-b0e3-fe2f43ea6ed1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that is incorporeal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "574d7a17-4f40-4afd-8a1b-d9d6f2b3e25e",
                                                "sense_id": "057fc5d1-b731-319a-9e0b-e38ad2bc3a13",
                                                "text": "The World is all viciſsitude and converſion. Nor is it onely true in Materials and Substances; but even in Spirits, in Incorporeals; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75b05514-3983-4dae-9cce-cb4f3b49b4ca",
                                                "sense_id": "057fc5d1-b731-319a-9e0b-e38ad2bc3a13",
                                                "text": "The divine nature of the celeſtial bodies cannot be ſeen through the teleſcope, and incorporeals are not to be viewed with a microſcopic eye: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b971dc46-06c1-45e6-8fc1-b151042f1227",
                                                "sense_id": "057fc5d1-b731-319a-9e0b-e38ad2bc3a13",
                                                "text": "Where the interest in a piece of land of one of six heirs to the deceased father’s estate was levied upon and it was claimed as a homestead, the Court said: “It is an incorporeal, and an incorporeal cannot be the object of the homestead act.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f667d5e-b0b9-49af-86b0-2777747192b0",
                                                "sense_id": "057fc5d1-b731-319a-9e0b-e38ad2bc3a13",
                                                "text": "It is manifest that incorporeals are incapable of transfer by delivery. But urban praedial rights may be ceded in court, and rural ones may also be mancipated."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
